  "guide": {
    "intro": [
      "Ubuntu is a Nguni Bantu word and ethic often translated as humanity toward others. Its core idea is that we only become fully human through relationship.",
      "It entered global conversation through Desmond Tutu and Nelson Mandela in South Africa’s transition from apartheid, and is now cited in ethics, leadership and software alike."
    ],
